<title>SOUTH AFRICA: OCEANA LIFTS HALF-YEAR YR SHR, DIV.</title>
<headline>OCEANA LIFTS HALF-YEAR YR SHR, DIV.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended March 31,</p>
<p>1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    29.3	  vs 24.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  7.0	  vs  6.1 cts     </p>
<p>    Attrib income	   40.45	 vs 25.55  </p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   60.46	 vs 42.99  </p>
<p>    Tax			 19.27	 vs 16.83   </p>
<p>    Interest received	1.21	 vs paid 1.80   </p>
<p>    Turnover		 497.12	 vs  387.94   </p>
<p>Div payable July 3 </p>
<p>on register June 6</p>
<p>Full name: Oceana Fishing Group Ltd </p>
<p>    Exceptional items     10.63	 vs  0.87    </p>
<p>NOTE - The group said that it expected a satisfactory</p>
<p>increase in earnings for the full year. Improved pilchard</p>
<p>volumes were expected to offset reduced fish meal volumes while</p>
<p>the trading and shipping divisions would continue to perform</p>
<p>well although not at the unusually high levels of the first six</p>
<p>months. The cold storage division was already experiencing</p>
<p>increased occupancy levels.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
